{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For it is his cloak alone.</b> והיא שמלתו is subordinate <b>to ערו</b> ('his skin'); then I warn you to return it to him. But if he has another, you are not warned. After it said שלמת רעך, which is feminine, it went back and said כי היא כסותה לבדה. <b>כסותה</b> means a covering with which one covers oneself at night." "<b>And it shall be that he cries out to Me.</b> To pray against you — that if you did not return his pledge, perhaps he would die of cold, and I will hear his prayer and repay you accordingly, <b>for I am gracious.</b> Another interpretation: <b>and I will hear, for I am gracious</b> — even though reason does not require you to return the pledge to him, since you lent your money on it and a creditor acquires the pledge, even so I will hear him, <b>for I am gracious</b>, and My compassion is stirred for him because he cried out before you and you were cruel and did not take pity on him. Therefore it says here <b>for I am gracious</b>; but above, regarding the orphan and widow, there is no need to write 'for I am gracious,' since you oppress them — it is justice that I should hear their cry."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:54.722374161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}